# General rules (Air Finance monorepo)

## Stack

- React 18, Vite 5, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS 3
- Yarn 4 workspaces + Turborepo
- Apps: `apps/web`, `apps/mobile-webview`; shared code: `packages/shared`
- Default branch: `main`
- Deploy: Vercel (see `docs/VERCEL_DEPLOY.md`)

## UI libraries

- Radix UI, Headless UI, lucide-react, sonner, recharts, framer-motion
- Prefer `class-variance-authority` (CVA) for component variants where used in the project

## State and data

- Server state: TanStack Query v5
- Client UI state: Zustand v5
- Forms: react-hook-form + zod

## Mobile-first

- Design and implement for small viewports first; enhance for tablet and desktop
- Touch targets, spacing, and navigation must work on mobile and WebView (`apps/mobile-webview`)

## TypeScript

- Do not use `any`
- Prefer `??` over `||` for nullish coalescing
- Mark component `props` as `readonly` (SonarQube typescript:S6759)

## Async

- Use `Promise.all` for independent async work; `Promise.allSettled` when partial failure is acceptable; `Promise.race` only when the first result wins

## Language

- Code, identifiers, and test descriptions in English
- User-facing copy follows product locale conventions

## Quality

- Avoid unnecessary comments
- Reuse existing patterns before adding new abstractions
- No simulated/mock data in dev or production paths (tests only)

## Migrated guidelines (from legacy `apps/web/.cursorrules`, adapted for web)

- Apply sensible component boundaries: keep visual components thin; move data and orchestration to hooks or route loaders
- Prefer custom hooks for reusable async and domain logic
- Use clear file names: PascalCase for components, `useX` for hooks, camelCase for utilities and services
- Treat errors explicitly; surface user-visible feedback via toasts or inline states as the project already does
- For list-heavy UIs, use virtualization patterns when lists are large (web equivalents of performant lists)
- New primary screens should use the existing layout shell (`ViewDefault` / `LayoutDefault` / `LayoutAuth` as appropriate to the route)
- Do not change visual or behavioral UX without explicit product justification
- Validate forms with zod schemas shared with types where possible
- Commit messages: conventional, in English (e.g. `feat(scope): summary`)
